/* book Worked example 2: Q: On 0 ≤ t ≤ 1 expand x(t) = t² in the shifted Legendre set φ₁ = 1, φ₂ = 2t − 1, φ₃ = 6t² − 6t + 1, with K₁ = 1, K₂ = 1/3, K₃ = 1/5. Find the coefficients, the error energy after two and after three terms, and check Parseval's relation.
   1. Energy of x: E = ∫₀¹ t⁴ dt = 1/5 = 0.2.
   2. c₁ = ∫₀¹ t² dt / 1 = 1/3.
   3. c₂ = ∫₀¹ t²(2t − 1) dt / (1/3) = (2/4 − 1/3)/(1/3) = (1/6)/(1/3) = 1/2.
   4. c₃ = ∫₀¹ t²(6t² − 6t + 1) dt / (1/5) = (6/5 − 6/4 + 1/3)/(1/5) = (1/30)(5) = 1/6.
   5. Energy carried by each term: c₁²K₁ = 1/9 ≈ 0.11111; c₂²K₂ = (1/4)(1/3) = 1/12 ≈ 0.08333; c₃²K₃ = (1/36)(1/5) = 1/180 ≈ 0.00556.
   6. Error energy after two terms: 1/5 − 1/9 − 1/12 = 1/180 ≈ 0.00556, about 2.8 % of E. After three terms: 1/180 − 1/180 = 0.
   7. Check: (1/3)(1) + (1/2)(2t − 1) + (1/6)(6t² − 6t + 1) = 1/3 + t − 1/2 + t² − t + 1/6 = t². Parseval: 1/9 + 1/12 + 1/180 = (20 + 15 + 1)/180 = 36/180 = 1/5 = E.
   Answer: c₁ = 1/3, c₂ = 1/2, c₃ = 1/6; error energy 1/180 ≈ 0.0056 after two terms and 0 after three; 1/9 + 1/12 + 1/180 = 1/5 = E. */
