/* book exam traps: Parseval's relation needs an orthogonal set. If ⟨φₘ, φₙ⟩ ≠ 0 the cross terms stay, and Σ |cₙ|²Kₙ is not the energy. | Multiply each |cₙ|² by Kₙ unless the set is orthonormal. For the sine set on (0, 2π), Kₙ = π; leaving it out gives Σ cₙ² = (16/π²)(π²/8) = 2 instead of the energy 2π. | Complete does not mean every finite sum is exact. The error reaches zero only in the limit: the square wave still has error energy 0.2538 after five nonzero terms. | Equality in energy is not equality at every point. At the jump t = π every sin nπ is 0, so the sine series gives 0, the midpoint of +1 and −1. */
